WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:09.600 position:63%
On this mountainous hillside in eastern
Java, I'm surrounded by hundreds, if not

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:14.640
thousands of coffee plants.
Coffee has been associated with

00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:18.570 position:59%
Indonesian history and economics for a
long time.

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:25.440 position:59%
Yet there's a crisis brewing here.
Environmental change is decreasing the

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:30.270 position:58%
crop and diluting the coffee.
And young Javanese would rather go to

00:00:30.270 --> 00:00:37.290 position:63%
college in big cities than work the land
as their forebears have java without its

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:40.200
namesake drink.
It's not out of the question.

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:44.970 position:58%
There aren't easy solutions.
Farms could move to higher and cooler

00:00:44.970 --> 00:00:49.120 position:61%
ground, but that land has to be bought.
You can't just march into it.

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:53.610
There's a role for science here.
Let's try to develop more climate

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:57.660 position:56%
resistant strains of coffee.
Given the popularity of drink at the

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:03.060 position:63%
start of many people's day, why not
develop a reserve of beans equivalent to

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:07.980 position:59%
the Strategic Petroleum Reserve in the
US or an IMF of caffeine?

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:13.260 position:63%
You don't want top decision makers to be
without their morning fix for too long.

